Mini Fixture Ground Truth

1. create_access_token is defined in auth/security.py.
2. Login flow: routers/auth.py:login calls verify_password, then calls
   create_access_token, both defined in auth/security.py.
3. JWT secret loading: config.py reads JWT_SECRET from the environment;
   auth/security.py:create_access_token uses it.
4. Authenticated item access: routers/items.py:list_items and create_item
   call auth/security.py:get_current_user.
5. Database setup: routers/items.py:list_items calls db.py:create_session.

Expected relationships include login -> verify_password,
login -> create_access_token, list_items -> get_current_user,
list_items -> create_session, and create_item -> get_current_user.
